<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Goryeong Gaya</h1><p class="st-meta">200 CE – 562 CE (approx.) · capital Hamchang</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the six Gaya polities named in Korean legend, of uncertain location and known almost entirely from later tradition.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goryeong">Goryeong</a> Gaya appears in the 13th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samguk-yusa">Samguk yusa</a> as one of the six Gaya states founded in 42 CE. That text places it at Hamchang, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangju">Sangju</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-gyeongsang-province">North Gyeongsang</a>, though some scholars doubt the identification.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from brief mentions in late sources, nothing reliable is recorded of its rulers or institutions. It should not be confused with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/daegaya">Daegaya</a>, whose capital was at the modern town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goryeong">Goryeong</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Like other Gaya polities it was absorbed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/silla">Silla</a>, probably by the 6th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/goryeong-gaya.jpg" alt="Goryeong Gaya" width="320" height="501"><figcaption>Image: Asieon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5th_century_Kaya_confederacy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>200 CE – 562 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hamchang</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaya language</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-korea">South Korea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hamchang Gaya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=381&amp;focus=goryeong-gaya" aria-label="Goryeong Gaya on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7927 906 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Goryeong Gaya lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8247 1162L8247 1162M8247 1162L8260 1139"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8247 1162h0M8260 1139h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8247 1162h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8247 1162h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=381&amp;focus=goryeong-gaya">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

